        <item>
            <title>2.0.13</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:01:05 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>20013</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.0.13</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>MotionUI 2.0.13</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Figma imports look more like Figma. Drop shadows keep their blend mode, so text in Apple's menu bar kit no longer gets a white glow, and shadows of see-through cards come out as strong as in Figma.</li>
  <li>Background blur on a single shape stays live in After Effects and follows the shape. 3D rotations from Figma arrive as live 3D, with the layers inside still editable.</li>
  <li>Fewer precomps: a shape with a gradient or an effect now arrives as one layer you can resize, not a precomp of its own.</li>
  <li>Very large soft glows, such as a huge blurred stroke behind a scene, arrive as an image of what the frame shows instead of a black layer. Shaders arrive as images.</li>
  <li>The animations in Learn are sharp on every screen, including monitors without Retina.</li>
  <li>The MotionUI panel opens a little wider, and the Figma plugin window has a slim dark scrollbar that only shows when the content is taller than the window.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
