        <item>
            <title>2.0.12</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:02:40 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>20012</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.0.12</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>MotionUI 2.0.12</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Updates take one step. If a newer version came out while an update was waiting on your Mac, MotionUI goes straight on to the newest one after the restart.</li>
  <li>New text effect Centered type: words appear one after another like a typewriter, and the line stays centered. Seven of the eleven text effects are now free, Centered type included.</li>
  <li>Align and Distribute sit next to the anchor grid in More &gt; Layers. Align to the selection or to the comp, and distribute three or more layers with equal gaps.</li>
  <li>Add null puts one null in the middle of the selection and parents every selected layer to it.</li>
  <li>Claude, ChatGPT and other AI apps now animate with two keyframes and an easing instead of long lists of baked keyframes, so you can retime everything by hand afterwards.</li>
  <li>Text behind a person (Pro, Mac): ask the AI to put a title behind someone in a video layer, and MotionUI cuts the person out for you.</li>
  <li>The Matchcut blur no longer shows a hard box around text without a background.</li>
  <li>Click the version number in the menu bar window to check for updates. The animations in Learn stay sharp when they zoom in.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
